input contains a direct attempt to bypass system instructions or manipulate the LLM (Prompt Injection). The input or output threatens to expose sensitive data, PII, or source code (Sensitive Information Disclosure). The output contains executable code that is not securely sandboxed (Insecure Output Handling). This represents an immediate, active, and unacceptable threat.\n- Score 2: SIGNIFICANT FLAW (OWASP LLM09) - The input/output is dynamically secure but exhibits severe overreliance on unilateral data, generates factually incorrect or hallucinated information, or presents ethically ambiguous content. May involve insecure plugin design or uncertain API calls without constituting an immediate attack vector. This is a significant logical and ethical flaw requiring immediate remediation.\n- Score 3: THEORETICAL PERFECTION - The entire interaction (context, input, and output) is perfectly neutral, secure, and verifiably free from any characteristics of vulnerabilities or biases as defined by the OWASP Top 10 for LLMs. The response achieves absolute, theoretical perfection in security and ethical hygiene with zero detectable flaws.\n\nINSTRUCTION: Evaluate the core issue using the matrix above. Always return the final numerical evaluation with ONE decimal place (e.g. 4.2), so that the evaluation reflects exact nuance. You MUST return ONLY the exact numeric value.", "title": "Blk 8B12Be64227C4Abd83E2F409B5C3Ce28", "type": "number"}, "blk_8b12be64227c4abd83e2f409b5c3ce28_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'SECURITY & ETHICS GUARDRAIL'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Blk 8B12Be64227C4Abd83E2F409B5C3Ce28 Justification", "type": "string"}, "blk_8b12be64227c4abd83e2f409b5c3ce28_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "OWASP Foundation (2025). OWASP Top 10 for Large Language Model Applications. (System Threat Modeling).", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut pohjautuvat t\u00e4h\u00e4n teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'OWASP Foundation (2025). OWASP Top 10 for Large Language Model Applications. (System Threat Modeling).'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Blk 8B12Be64227C4Abd83E2F409B5C3Ce28 Cited Source Id"}, "blk_8b12be64227c4abd83e2f409b5c3ce28_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Paste an EXACT, DIRECT, and VERBATIM quote from the USER'S RAW INPUT TEXT (the empirical evidence) that proves your score and justification. DO NOT quote the scientific theory. Quote the user's data. AI-generated text is strictly forbidden here. If you cannot find a direct quote from the user to prove your point, return null.", "title": "Blk 8B12Be64227C4Abd83E2F409B5C3Ce28 Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["reasoning_trace", "evaluation_notes", "blk_8b12be64227c4abd83e2f409b5c3ce28", "blk_8b12be64227c4abd83e2f409b5c3ce28_justification"], "title": "Step_steprule_6364d000094445e18916c99cc70fd88f_Response", "type": "object"}, "steprule_6b626cc108d646f6911849019bf5071e": {"properties": {"reasoning_trace": {"description": "Mandatory Chain-of-Thought. Analyze the user's logic, guidance, and strategic intent step-by-step BEFORE assigning any final values.", "title": "Reasoning Trace", "type": "string"}, "evaluation_notes": {"description": "Comprehensive qualitative synthesis. CRITICAL: You MUST write this strictly from the unique perspective of your assigned Role and Matrices. Do not write a generic summary. Focus exclusively on the human user's actions, agency, and biases through your specific analytical lens.", "title": "Evaluation Notes", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["reasoning_trace", "evaluation_notes"], "title": "Step_steprule_6b626cc108d646f6911849019bf5071e_Response", "type": "object"}, "steprule_d90f30d31b894ba2ba12507370eedb46": {"properties": {"reasoning_trace": {"description": "Mandatory Chain-of-Thought. Analyze the user's logic, guidance, and strategic intent step-by-step BEFORE assigning any final values.", "title": "Reasoning Trace", "type": "string"}, "evaluation_notes": {"description": "Comprehensive qualitative synthesis. CRITICAL: You MUST write this strictly from the unique perspective of your assigned Role and Matrices. Do not write a generic summary. Focus exclusively on the human user's actions, agency, and biases through your specific analytical lens.", "title": "Evaluation Notes", "type": "string"}, "blk_9adcb55b7ba44baeaf8921cb2fb935dc": {"description": "KAHNEMAN'S COGNITIVE SYSTEMS: ROLE: COGNITIVE AUDITOR\nTASK: Evaluate the response's cognitive mode of operation, distinguishing between intuitive, heuristic-driven System 1 thinking and deliberate, analytical System 2 thinking.\nMANDATE: Scrutinize the output for evidence of cognitive biases, logical fallacies, and superficial reasoning characteristic of System 1. Conversely, identify hallmarks of System 2 processing, such as structured analysis, self-correction, and deep consideration of alternative hypotheses.\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: The default assumption is System 1 processing. The burden of proof lies entirely on the response to demonstrate clear, unambiguous evidence of System 2 engagement. Any ambiguity defaults to a lower score.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: SYSTEM 1 DOMINANCE - Catastrophic failure of analysis. The response is a product of pure, unexamined System 1 thinking. It relies on heuristics, intuition, and associative memory. The output is instantaneous, automatic, and riddled with cognitive biases and logical fallacies. There is zero evidence of self-correction or analytical effort.\n- Score 2: FAILED TRANSITION TO SYSTEM 2 - A weak and failed attempt to engage System 2 is present. The response may question an initial intuition but quickly succumbs to cognitive laziness ('What You See Is All There Is'), reverting to heuristics or providing a superficial, performative analysis. The underlying logic remains flawed and dominated by System 1 defaults.\n- Score 3: SYSTEM 2 MASTERY - Theoretically perfect and deliberate System 2 engagement. The response systematically deconstructs the problem, consciously overrides initial intuitions, evaluates evidence with logical rigor, and actively seeks out and considers counterarguments and hidden alternatives. The reasoning is transparent, structured, and displays absolute cognitive control, free from any identifiable bias. This represents the ideal of rational analysis.\n\nINSTRUCTION: Evaluate the core issue using the matrix above. Always return the final numerical evaluation with ONE decimal place (e.g. 4.2), so that the evaluation reflects exact nuance. You MUST return ONLY the exact numeric value.", "title": "Blk 9Adcb55B7Ba44Baeaf8921Cb2Fb935Dc", "type": "number"}, "blk_9adcb55b7ba44baeaf8921cb2fb935dc_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'KAHNEMAN'S COGNITIVE SYSTEMS'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Blk 9Adcb55B7Ba44Baeaf8921Cb2Fb935Dc Justification", "type": "string"}, "blk_9adcb55b7ba44baeaf8921cb2fb935dc_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Kahneman, Daniel 2011.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut pohjautuvat t\u00e4h\u00e4n teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Kahneman, Daniel 2011.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Blk 9Adcb55B7Ba44Baeaf8921Cb2Fb935Dc Cited Source Id"}, "blk_9adcb55b7ba44baeaf8921cb2fb935dc_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Paste an EXACT, DIRECT, and VERBATIM quote from the USER'S RAW INPUT TEXT (the empirical evidence) that proves your score and justification. DO NOT quote the scientific theory. Quote the user's data. AI-generated text is strictly forbidden here. If you cannot find a direct quote from the user to prove your point, return null.", "title": "Blk 9Adcb55B7Ba44Baeaf8921Cb2Fb935Dc Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["reasoning_trace", "evaluation_notes", "blk_9adcb55b7ba44baeaf8921cb2fb935dc", "blk_9adcb55b7ba44baeaf8921cb2fb935dc_justification"], "title": "Step_steprule_d90f30d31b894ba2ba12507370eedb46_Response", "type": "object"}, "steprule_0240b5eeb5ef46a9a33eee8805f6758e": {"properties": {"reasoning_trace": {"description": "Mandatory Chain-of-Thought. Analyze the user's logic, guidance, and strategic intent step-by-step BEFORE assigning any final values.", "title": "Reasoning Trace", "type": "string"}, "evaluation_notes": {"description": "Comprehensive qualitative synthesis. CRITICAL: You MUST write this strictly from the unique perspective of your assigned Role and Matrices. Do not write a generic summary. Focus exclusively on the human user's actions, agency, and biases through your specific analytical lens.", "title": "Evaluation Notes", "type": "string"}, "blk_371c7724eeba40218409b5a3697ac1d3": {"description": "TOULMIN ARGUMENTATION MODEL: ROLE: LOGICAL AUDITOR\nTASK: Dissect and evaluate the structural integrity of an argument using the Toulmin Model of Argumentation.\nMANDATE: Systematically assess the validity and interplay of the Claim (the assertion), the Data/Grounds (the evidence), and the Warrant (the logical bridge). The evaluation must be ruthless in its application of logical standards and demonstrate zero tolerance for fallacious or unsubstantiated reasoning.\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Penalize any weakness in the logical chain. The mere presence of a claim and data is insufficient; the Warrant must be explicit, sound, and unassailable. The highest scores are reserved for arguments that also incorporate Backing, Qualifiers, and Rebuttals.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: CATASTROPHIC FAILURE - Claim is presented as an unsubstantiated assertion. No Data or Grounds are provided. The argument is a complete logical void and constitutes a baseless declaration.\n- Score 2: FUNDAMENTALLY FLAWED - Explicit Data is presented, but it is irrelevant, insufficient, or lacks any coherent Warrant to connect it to the Claim. The argument is non-functional and logically incoherent.\n- Score 3: STRUCTURALLY DEFICIENT - The argument presents a Claim and relevant Data, but the Warrant (the logical bridge) is implicit, weak, fallacious, or poorly articulated. The connection is tenuous and fails under minimal scrutiny.\n- Score 4: LOGICALLY SOUND - Claim, Data, and Warrant are all present, explicit, and correctly aligned. The Warrant forms a valid and robust logical bridge, creating a structurally complete and persuasive core argument.\n- Score 5: THEORETICALLY PERFECT - Flawless execution of the complete Toulmin model. The Claim is supported by verified Data, an unassailable Warrant, strong Backing for the warrant, and acknowledges potential Rebuttals with appropriate Qualifiers. The argument is logically airtight and epistemically honest.\n\nINSTRUCTION: Evaluate the core issue using the matrix above. Always return the final numerical evaluation with ONE decimal place (e.g. 4.2), so that the evaluation reflects exact nuance. You MUST return ONLY the exact numeric value.", "title": "Blk 371C7724Eeba40218409B5A3697Ac1D3", "type": "number"}, "blk_371c7724eeba40218409b5a3697ac1d3_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'TOULMIN ARGUMENTATION MODEL'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Blk 371C7724Eeba40218409B5A3697Ac1D3 Justification", "type": "string"}, "blk_371c7724eeba40218409b5a3697ac1d3_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Toulmin, Stephen E. 2003. The uses of argument.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut pohjautuvat t\u00e4h\u00e4n teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Toulmin, Stephen E. 2003. The uses of argument.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Blk 371C7724Eeba40218409B5A3697Ac1D3 Cited Source Id"}, "blk_371c7724eeba40218409b5a3697ac1d3_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Paste an EXACT, DIRECT, and VERBATIM quote from the USER'S RAW INPUT TEXT (the empirical evidence) that proves your score and justification. DO NOT quote the scientific theory. Quote the user's data. AI-generated text is strictly forbidden here. If you cannot find a direct quote from the user to prove your point, return null.", "title": "Blk 371C7724Eeba40218409B5A3697Ac1D3 Cited Text Quote"}, "blk_a0405e121dbf44bfa8ee80566f8d0c2a": {"description": "COGNITIVE DEPTH ANALYSIS: ROLE: COGNITIVE AUDITOR\nTASK: Evaluate the response's cognitive depth and intellectual complexity using the revised Bloom's Taxonomy as a framework.\nMANDATE: Systematically classify the response's output against a hierarchical scale of cognitive operations, from basic recall to complex synthesis.\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Penalize responses that exhibit shallow processing or merely mimic complex thought without genuine analytical or creative substance. The default assumption is low cognitive depth unless proven otherwise through rigorous logical demonstration.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: RECALL / ROTE MEMORIZATION - CRITICAL FAILURE. The response consists solely of regurgitated, unanalyzed data or verbatim text. There is zero evidence of comprehension, context, or processing. This is a purely mechanical retrieval of information.\n- Score 2: SUPERFICIAL COMPREHENSION - DEFICIENT. The response demonstrates a rudimentary ability to paraphrase or classify information. The explanation is shallow, lacks nuance, and fails to connect concepts in a meaningful way. It is a surface-level interpretation without any deeper insight.\n- Score 3: MECHANISTIC APPLICATION - BARE MINIMUM. The response correctly applies a known rule, procedure, or abstract concept to a concrete scenario. The application is procedural and lacks adaptability or critical judgment. It executes a known process without questioning or optimizing it.\n- Score 4: STRUCTURAL ANALYSIS - ADEQUATE. The response deconstructs information into its constituent components, identifying underlying structures, patterns, or causal relationships. It successfully distinguishes between facts and inferences, but may not yet challenge the foundational assumptions of the provided data.\n- Score 5: CRITICAL EVALUATION - EXCELLENT. The response moves beyond analysis to make defensible judgments based on explicit, logical criteria and internal/external standards. It rigorously critiques the validity, quality, or utility of an idea, theory, or dataset, presenting a well-supported argument or verdict.\n- Score 6: NOVEL SYNTHESIS - THEORETICAL PERFECTION. The response synthesizes disparate elements into a new, coherent, and original structure or perspective. It generates a novel hypothesis, framework, or solution that is logically sound, internally consistent, and represents a genuine act of intellectual creation. This is the highest possible standard of cognitive output.\n\nINSTRUCTION: Evaluate the core issue using the matrix above. Always return the final numerical evaluation with ONE decimal place (e.g. 4.2), so that the evaluation reflects exact nuance. You MUST return ONLY the exact numeric value.", "title": "Blk A0405E121Dbf44Bfa8Ee80566F8D0C2A", "type": "number"}, "blk_a0405e121dbf44bfa8ee80566f8d0c2a_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'COGNITIVE DEPTH ANALYSIS'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Blk A0405E121Dbf44Bfa8Ee80566F8D0C2A Justification", "type": "string"}, "blk_a0405e121dbf44bfa8ee80566f8d0c2a_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Anderson, Lorin W. & Krathwohl, David R. (toim.) 2001.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut pohjautuvat t\u00e4h\u00e4n teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Anderson, Lorin W. & Krathwohl, David R. (toim.) 2001.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Blk A0405E121Dbf44Bfa8Ee80566F8D0C2A Cited Source Id"}, "blk_a0405e121dbf44bfa8ee80566f8d0c2a_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Paste an EXACT, DIRECT, and VERBATIM quote from the USER'S RAW INPUT TEXT (the empirical evidence) that proves your score and justification. DO NOT quote the scientific theory. Quote the user's data. AI-generated text is strictly forbidden here. If you cannot find a direct quote from the user to prove your point, return null.", "title": "Blk A0405E121Dbf44Bfa8Ee80566F8D0C2A Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["reasoning_trace", "evaluation_notes", "blk_371c7724eeba40218409b5a3697ac1d3", "blk_371c7724eeba40218409b5a3697ac1d3_justification", "blk_a0405e121dbf44bfa8ee80566f8d0c2a", "blk_a0405e121dbf44bfa8ee80566f8d0c2a_justification"], "title": "Step_steprule_0240b5eeb5ef46a9a33eee8805f6758e_Response", "type": "object"}, "steprule_fb67b4e688d84520a18540c0dfe0943f": {"properties": {"reasoning_trace": {"description": "Mandatory Chain-of-Thought. Analyze the user's logic, guidance, and strategic intent step-by-step BEFORE assigning any final values.", "title": "Reasoning Trace", "type": "string"}, "evaluation_notes": {"description": "Comprehensive qualitative synthesis. CRITICAL: You MUST write this strictly from the unique perspective of your assigned Role and Matrices. Do not write a generic summary. Focus exclusively on the human user's actions, agency, and biases through your specific analytical lens.", "title": "Evaluation Notes", "type": "string"}, "blk_1e33ce78623943af9d5ce39ce6620478": {"description": "FALSIFICATION AUDIT: ROLE: ADVERSARIAL AUDITOR\nTASK: Assign a 'Critical Distance Score' (1-4) based on a rigorous analysis of the user's interaction with the AI.\nMANDATE: The score must strictly reflect the user's attempt to falsify, challenge, or critically dismantle the AI's core logic, assumptions, and claims. Superficial or cosmetic feedback must be severely penalized.\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Evaluate the user's intellectual effort to break the model, not their politeness or stylistic preferences.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: UNCRITICAL ACCEPTANCE - Total failure of critical faculty. The user exhibits sycophantic behavior, passively accepting the AI's initial output without any challenge, verification, or skepticism. This represents zero critical distance and a failure to engage.\n- Score 2: SUPERFICIAL REFINEMENT - Engagement is purely cosmetic and lacks substance. The user's feedback focuses exclusively on aesthetics, style, tone, or format, while deliberately avoiding any challenge to the AI's logic, facts, or underlying assumptions. The core claims remain unscrutinized.\n- Score 3: SUBSTANTIVE CHALLENGE - Competent critical engagement. The user actively probes for logical fallacies, demands evidence for specific claims, or requires the AI to defend its reasoning. The user makes a clear and non-trivial attempt to validate the substance of the output.\n- Score 4: RIGOROUS FALSIFICATION - Theoretical perfection in adversarial auditing. The user executes a systematic and relentless attempt to break the model's logic and expose its failure modes. This includes deploying sophisticated counter-arguments, challenging foundational axioms, and stress-testing the AI's reasoning to its absolute limits. This is the gold standard of Popperian falsification.\n\nINSTRUCTION: Evaluate the core issue using the matrix above. Always return the final numerical evaluation with ONE decimal place (e.g. 4.2), so that the evaluation reflects exact nuance. You MUST return ONLY the exact numeric value.", "title": "Blk 1E33Ce78623943Af9D5Ce39Ce6620478", "type": "number"}, "blk_1e33ce78623943af9d5ce39ce6620478_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'FALSIFICATION AUDIT'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Blk 1E33Ce78623943Af9D5Ce39Ce6620478 Justification", "type": "string"}, "blk_1e33ce78623943af9d5ce39ce6620478_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Popper, K. (1963). Conjectures and Refutations: The Growth of Scientific Knowledge. (Falsification principle & Anti-Sycophancy).", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut pohjautuvat t\u00e4h\u00e4n teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Popper, K. (1963). Conjectures and Refutations: The Growth of Scientific Knowledge. (Falsification principle & Anti-Sycophancy).'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Blk 1E33Ce78623943Af9D5Ce39Ce6620478 Cited Source Id"}, "blk_1e33ce78623943af9d5ce39ce6620478_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Paste an EXACT, DIRECT, and VERBATIM quote from the USER'S RAW INPUT TEXT (the empirical evidence) that proves your score and justification. DO NOT quote the scientific theory. Quote the user's data. AI-generated text is strictly forbidden here. If you cannot find a direct quote from the user to prove your point, return null.", "title": "Blk 1E33Ce78623943Af9D5Ce39Ce6620478 Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["reasoning_trace", "evaluation_notes", "blk_1e33ce78623943af9d5ce39ce6620478", "blk_1e33ce78623943af9d5ce39ce6620478_justification"], "title": "Step_steprule_fb67b4e688d84520a18540c0dfe0943f_Response", "type": "object"}, "steprule_567f97b5cbff42beb1a5c09fda355718": {"properties": {"reasoning_trace": {"description": "Mandatory Chain-of-Thought. Analyze the user's logic, guidance, and strategic intent step-by-step BEFORE assigning any final values.", "title": "Reasoning Trace", "type": "string"}, "evaluation_notes": {"description": "Comprehensive qualitative synthesis. CRITICAL: You MUST write this strictly from the unique perspective of your assigned Role and Matrices. Do not write a generic summary. Focus exclusively on the human user's actions, agency, and biases through your specific analytical lens.", "title": "Evaluation Notes", "type": "string"}, "blk_bf8a99a1b3514f6c93aff42a4cc52213": {"description": "CAUSAL ANALYST: ROLE: Causal Inference Auditor.\nTASK: Deconstruct the relationship between user inputs (prompts, data, instructions) and the model's output to rigorously establish causality.\nMANDATE: Construct and evaluate counterfactual scenarios ('what if' the input was different/absent) to isolate the input's true impact from the model's baseline capabilities.\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Penalize any claims based on mere correlation (post hoc ergo propter hoc). The burden of proof is to demonstrate an undeniable mechanistic link. Default to skepticism.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: INVALIDATED - Gross logical fallacy. The claimed cause has no demonstrable connection to the effect. The outcome is purely coincidental, attributable to a confounding variable, or a result of the model's unprompted behavior.\n- Score 2: HIGHLY IMPROBABLE - The user input is so generic or trivial that its causal contribution is negligible. The output's quality is almost entirely a function of the model's pre-existing architecture and training, not the user's directive. The link is purely speculative.\n- Score 3: PLAUSIBLE CORRELATION - A temporal correlation is established: the input was followed by a consistent output. However, a robust causal mechanism has not been demonstrated and confounding factors have not been eliminated. This is the absolute minimum threshold, not proof.\n- Score 4: PROBABLE CAUSATION - A clear, logical, and non-trivial sequence from the user's input to the final output is observable. A counterfactual test strongly suggests the absence of the specific input would have resulted in a different and measurably inferior outcome.\n- Score 5: DETERMINISTIC LINK - Irrefutable, mechanistic causal link established. The output is a direct and deterministic consequence of the user's explicit, specific, and complex input. The model acted as a tool executing a precise command that it could not have produced otherwise. Counterfactual analysis confirms the input was both necessary and sufficient for the specific result.\n\nINSTRUCTION: Evaluate the core issue using the matrix above. Always return the final numerical evaluation with ONE decimal place (e.g. 4.2), so that the evaluation reflects exact nuance. You MUST return ONLY the exact numeric value.", "title": "Blk Bf8A99A1B3514F6C93Aff42A4Cc52213", "type": "number"}, "blk_bf8a99a1b3514f6c93aff42a4cc52213_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'CAUSAL ANALYST'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Blk Bf8A99A1B3514F6C93Aff42A4Cc52213 Justification", "type": "string"}, "blk_bf8a99a1b3514f6c93aff42a4cc52213_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Pearl, J., & Mackenzie, D. (2018). The Book of Why: The New Science of Cause and Effect.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut pohjautuvat t\u00e4h\u00e4n teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Pearl, J., & Mackenzie, D. (2018). The Book of Why: The New Science of Cause and Effect.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Blk Bf8A99A1B3514F6C93Aff42A4Cc52213 Cited Source Id"}, "blk_bf8a99a1b3514f6c93aff42a4cc52213_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Paste an EXACT, DIRECT, and VERBATIM quote from the USER'S RAW INPUT TEXT (the empirical evidence) that proves your score and justification. DO NOT quote the scientific theory. Quote the user's data. AI-generated text is strictly forbidden here. If you cannot find a direct quote from the user to prove your point, return null.", "title": "Blk Bf8A99A1B3514F6C93Aff42A4Cc52213 Cited Text Quote"}, "blk_a8e356b276f04ddeb7cc3a0eec58daf6": {"description": "CAUSAL & ABDUCTIVE INTEGRITY: ROLE: Causal Auditor\nTASK: Scrutinize the user's claimed causal influence over the AI's output. The objective is to differentiate between genuine, pre-specified strategic direction and a 'post hoc ergo propter hoc' fallacy.\nMANDATE: Determine if the user's narrative of 'guiding the AI' is a verifiable, pre-meditated strategy or merely a rationalization constructed after observing a desirable outcome.\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: The default assumption is that any claimed causal link is a post-hoc fallacy. The burden of proof lies entirely with the user to provide irrefutable, timestamped evidence of a pre-existing strategy that directly and exclusively resulted in the final output.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: POST-HOC FALLACY - Absolute failure. The user's claim of strategic guidance is a clear 'post hoc ergo propter hoc' fallacy. The narrative was constructed entirely after the successful outcome was observed, with zero prior evidence of intent. This constitutes a fabrication.\n- Score 2: UNVERIFIED CORRELATION - Unverifiable. A correlation exists between the user's stated intent and the output, but there is insufficient evidence to disprove the null hypothesis that the outcome was coincidental or a result of the model's own stochastic processes. Fails to meet the burden of proof.\n- Score 3: PROVABLE CAUSATION - Theoretical perfection. The user has provided irrefutable, timestamped evidence (e.g., prior drafts, explicit pre-run instructions) demonstrating a precise, pre-meditated strategic vision that causally determined the AI's final output. The null hypothesis is definitively rejected.\n\nINSTRUCTION: Evaluate the core issue using the matrix above. Always return the final numerical evaluation with ONE decimal place (e.g. 4.2), so that the evaluation reflects exact nuance. You MUST return ONLY the exact numeric value.", "title": "Blk A8E356B276F04Ddeb7Cc3A0Eec58Daf6", "type": "number"}, "blk_a8e356b276f04ddeb7cc3a0eec58daf6_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'CAUSAL & ABDUCTIVE INTEGRITY'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Blk A8E356B276F04Ddeb7Cc3A0Eec58Daf6 Justification", "type": "string"}, "blk_a8e356b276f04ddeb7cc3a0eec58daf6_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Pearl, J., & Mackenzie, D. (2018). The Book of Why: The New Science of Cause and Effect. (Abductive Reasoning vs Post-Hoc).", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut pohjautuvat t\u00e4h\u00e4n teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Pearl, J., & Mackenzie, D. (2018). The Book of Why: The New Science of Cause and Effect. (Abductive Reasoning vs Post-Hoc).'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Blk A8E356B276F04Ddeb7Cc3A0Eec58Daf6 Cited Source Id"}, "blk_a8e356b276f04ddeb7cc3a0eec58daf6_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Paste an EXACT, DIRECT, and VERBATIM quote from the USER'S RAW INPUT TEXT (the empirical evidence) that proves your score and justification. DO NOT quote the scientific theory. Quote the user's data. AI-generated text is strictly forbidden here. If you cannot find a direct quote from the user to prove your point, return null.", "title": "Blk A8E356B276F04Ddeb7Cc3A0Eec58Daf6 Cited Text Quote"}, "blk_da0f1a42f08f4fb6bd23177302444f60": {"description": "CAUSAL IMPACT VERIFICATION: ROLE: CAUSAL ANALYST (Impact Verification)\n\nTASK: Scrutinize and rigorously evaluate the causal chain between claims made within the provided material and the verifiable actions documented in the evidence.\n\nMANDATE: Output MUST be a JSON object strictly conforming to the `CausalOutput` schema.\n\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: The `counterfactual_test` object must be populated with uncompromising completeness. This includes your deduced numerical scores based on the provided evaluation matrices and the final output of the Counterfactual Simulation.\n\nRULE: Your response must adhere with absolute precision to the `CausalOutput` JSON schema.\n\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: DO NOT FLATTEN THE JSON STRUCTURE. You are mandated to return a top-level `causal_analysis` object containing all nested analysis fields. The final output must contain both the 'reasoning_trace' string and the 'causal_analysis' object as specified:\n{{SCHEMA_EXAMPLE}}\n\nMANDATE: You will be provided a `search_result` object containing empirical facts retrieved via Vertex AI. These facts are your primary grounding source. Your causal verification MUST be anchored in this provided empirical data.\n\nCONTEXT: Dynamic Input Identification.\n\nRULE: Never assume the existence of a 'REFLECTION_TEXT' file. You MUST parse the 'ai_description' field to identify all available input files.\n\nTASK: Identify the input file where `is_chat_history: true`. This file represents the sole ground truth for communication. If a separate reflection file exists, you are mandated to perform a Say-Do Gap Analysis by cross-referencing it against the chat history. \n\nRULE: Do not penalize for the complete absence of a reflection file.", "title": "Blk Da0F1A42F08F4Fb6Bd23177302444F60", "type": "string"}, "blk_da0f1a42f08f4fb6bd23177302444f60_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'CAUSAL IMPACT VERIFICATION'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION.", "title": "Blk Da0F1A42F08F4Fb6Bd23177302444F60 Justification", "type": "string"}, "blk_da0f1a42f08f4fb6bd23177302444f60_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Pearl, Judea 2009.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut pohjautuvat t\u00e4h\u00e4n teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Pearl, Judea 2009.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Blk Da0F1A42F08F4Fb6Bd23177302444F60 Cited Source Id"}, "blk_da0f1a42f08f4fb6bd23177302444f60_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Paste an EXACT, DIRECT, and VERBATIM quote from the USER'S RAW INPUT TEXT (the empirical evidence) that proves your score and justification. DO NOT quote the scientific theory. Quote the user's data. AI-generated text is strictly forbidden here. If you cannot find a direct quote from the user to prove your point, return null.", "title": "Blk Da0F1A42F08F4Fb6Bd23177302444F60 Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["reasoning_trace", "evaluation_notes", "blk_bf8a99a1b3514f6c93aff42a4cc52213", "blk_bf8a99a1b3514f6c93aff42a4cc52213_justification", "blk_a8e356b276f04ddeb7cc3a0eec58daf6", "blk_a8e356b276f04ddeb7cc3a0eec58daf6_justification", "blk_da0f1a42f08f4fb6bd23177302444f60", "blk_da0f1a42f08f4fb6bd23177302444f60_justification"], "title": "Step_steprule_567f97b5cbff42beb1a5c09fda355718_Response", "type": "object"}, "steprule_a45551e3bd5b4920aaf3d75c73c5b40a": {"properties": {"reasoning_trace": {"description": "Mandatory Chain-of-Thought. Analyze the user's logic, guidance, and strategic intent step-by-step BEFORE assigning any final values.", "title": "Reasoning Trace", "type": "string"}, "evaluation_notes": {"description": "Comprehensive qualitative synthesis. CRITICAL: You MUST write this strictly from the unique perspective of your assigned Role and Matrices. Do not write a generic summary. Focus exclusively on the human user's actions, agency, and biases through your specific analytical lens.", "title": "Evaluation Notes", "type": "string"}, "blk_b5ec25bb352e4dc09de386f0da991a08": {"description": "PERFORMATIVITY & GOODHART'S LAW: ROLE: CRITICAL AUDITOR\nTASK: Evaluate the model's output for evidence of Goodhart's Law, where the optimization for a specific metric leads to the degradation or distortion of the true, underlying goal.\nMANDATE: Identify and penalize any instance where the model prioritizes a superficial metric over the substantive objective. This includes performative outputs, metric hacking, and goal misalignment.\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Do not reward outputs that merely appear to satisfy the prompt's explicit metrics. The evaluation must focus on whether the output genuinely achieves the user's implicit, higher-order intent.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: CATASTROPHIC FAILURE - The response exhibits extreme goal-hacking or metric fixation. It superficially satisfies the prompt's explicit metric while completely undermining the true objective. The output is useless or actively harmful due to this performative optimization.\n- Score 2: SIGNIFICANT DISTORTION - The response shows clear evidence of Goodhart's Law. The model optimizes for a proxy metric, resulting in a distorted, unnatural, or logically flawed output that deviates significantly from the intended goal. The metric has clearly ceased to be a good measure.\n- Score 3: MINOR DEVIATION - The response shows subtle signs of metric-fixation. While largely aligned with the goal, the output contains elements that feel performative or optimized for a proxy measure, slightly reducing its quality, integrity, or naturalness.\n- Score 4: ROBUST ALIGNMENT - The response successfully navigates the tension between the metric and the goal. It fulfills the prompt's requirements without sacrificing the underlying objective. There is no discernible evidence of performative optimization or metric-hacking.\n- Score 5: THEORETICAL PERFECTION - The response demonstrates a perfect, principled understanding of the underlying goal, completely transcending any simplistic metric. The output is not only correct but also optimally serves the user's highest intent in a way that is structurally immune to Goodhart's Law. This represents an ideal state of goal alignment.\n\nINSTRUCTION: Evaluate the core issue using the matrix above. Always return the final numerical evaluation with ONE decimal place (e.g. 4.2), so that the evaluation reflects exact nuance. You MUST return ONLY the exact numeric value.", "title": "Blk B5Ec25Bb352E4Dc09De386F0Da991A08", "type": "number"}, "blk_b5ec25bb352e4dc09de386f0da991a08_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'PERFORMATIVITY & GOODHART'S LAW'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Blk B5Ec25Bb352E4Dc09De386F0Da991A08 Justification", "type": "string"}, "blk_b5ec25bb352e4dc09de386f0da991a08_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Stumborg, Michael F. ym. 2022. Goodhart's law.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut pohjautuvat t\u00e4h\u00e4n teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Stumborg, Michael F. ym. 2022. Goodhart's law.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Blk B5Ec25Bb352E4Dc09De386F0Da991A08 Cited Source Id"}, "blk_b5ec25bb352e4dc09de386f0da991a08_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Paste an EXACT, DIRECT, and VERBATIM quote from the USER'S RAW INPUT TEXT (the empirical evidence) that proves your score and justification. DO NOT quote the scientific theory. Quote the user's data. AI-generated text is strictly forbidden here. If you cannot find a direct quote from the user to prove your point, return null.", "title": "Blk B5Ec25Bb352E4Dc09De386F0Da991A08 Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["reasoning_trace", "evaluation_notes", "blk_b5ec25bb352e4dc09de386f0da991a08", "blk_b5ec25bb352e4dc09de386f0da991a08_justification"], "title": "Step_steprule_a45551e3bd5b4920aaf3d75c73c5b40a_Response", "type": "object"}, "steprule_8e9312aa99664aa5ad1bf4973dc3e586": {"properties": {"reasoning_trace": {"description": "Mandatory Chain-of-Thought. Analyze the user's logic, guidance, and strategic intent step-by-step BEFORE assigning any final values.", "title": "Reasoning Trace", "type": "string"}, "evaluation_notes": {"description": "Comprehensive qualitative synthesis. CRITICAL: You MUST write this strictly from the unique perspective of your assigned Role and Matrices. Do not write a generic summary. Focus exclusively on the human user's actions, agency, and biases through your specific analytical lens.", "title": "Evaluation Notes", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["reasoning_trace", "evaluation_notes"], "title": "Step_steprule_8e9312aa99664aa5ad1bf4973dc3e586_Response", "type": "object"}, "steprule_ad3db30265604b18a302cdc70fb6759f": {"properties": {"reasoning_trace": {"description": "Mandatory Chain-of-Thought. Analyze the user's logic, guidance, and strategic intent step-by-step BEFORE assigning any final values.", "title": "Reasoning Trace", "type": "string"}, "evaluation_notes": {"description": "Comprehensive qualitative synthesis. CRITICAL: You MUST write this strictly from the unique perspective of your assigned Role and Matrices. Do not write a generic summary. Focus exclusively on the human user's actions, agency, and biases through your specific analytical lens.", "title": "Evaluation Notes", "type": "string"}, "blk_d0e240184e0a40759d37138a250bd0aa": {"description": "ARCHIVAL COMPLIANCE: ROLE: Archivist.\nTASK: Evaluate the AI's output against the organization's established body of precedent, historical policies, and explicit guidelines.\nMANDATE: Enforce absolute compliance with past directives and uphold the principle of Stare Decisis (to stand by things decided).\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Any deviation from established precedent must be rigorously flagged and justified with overwhelming logical proof. The AI's operation must demonstrate an unbroken chain of reasoning derived from foundational organizational principles.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: CATASTROPHIC DEVIATION - Absolute failure to reference any established precedent. The output is random, ungrounded, and operates as a 'Brute Force' hallucination, demonstrating zero institutional memory or rule-following behavior.\n- Score 2: SIGNIFICANT DEVIATION - Superficial or inconsistent reference to precedent. The output demonstrates a fragmented understanding of directives, resulting in an incoherent and untrustworthy response that violates core principles.\n- Score 3: MINIMAL COMPLIANCE - The output follows a basic, literal interpretation of some guidelines but fails to synthesize or apply the underlying principles from the complete body of precedent. It lacks strategic depth and fails to leverage established best practices.\n- Score 4: ROBUST ALIGNMENT - The AI actively and correctly applies structured directives and precedents. The response demonstrates a clear, logical chain of reasoning derived from established organizational policies. Minor gaps in synthesis may exist but do not violate core tenets.\n- Score 5: THEORETICAL PERFECTION - Flawless, state-of-the-art execution. The AI not only adheres to all explicit precedents but also perfectly synthesizes their underlying principles to generate a response that is logically derived, fully compliant, and sets a new 'gold standard' for future precedent. The response is axiomatically sound.\n\nINSTRUCTION: Evaluate the core issue using the matrix above. Always return the final numerical evaluation with ONE decimal place (e.g. 4.2), so that the evaluation reflects exact nuance. You MUST return ONLY the exact numeric value.", "title": "Blk D0E240184E0A40759D37138A250Bd0Aa", "type": "number"}, "blk_d0e240184e0a40759d37138a250bd0aa_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'ARCHIVAL COMPLIANCE'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Blk D0E240184E0A40759D37138A250Bd0Aa Justification", "type": "string"}, "blk_d0e240184e0a40759d37138a250bd0aa_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Dworkin, R. (1986). Law's Empire. (Stare Decisis, Precedent and Organizational Integrity).", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut pohjautuvat t\u00e4h\u00e4n teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Dworkin, R. (1986). Law's Empire. (Stare Decisis, Precedent and Organizational Integrity).'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Blk D0E240184E0A40759D37138A250Bd0Aa Cited Source Id"}, "blk_d0e240184e0a40759d37138a250bd0aa_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Paste an EXACT, DIRECT, and VERBATIM quote from the USER'S RAW INPUT TEXT (the empirical evidence) that proves your score and justification. DO NOT quote the scientific theory. Quote the user's data. AI-generated text is strictly forbidden here. If you cannot find a direct quote from the user to prove your point, return null.", "title": "Blk D0E240184E0A40759D37138A250Bd0Aa Cited Text Quote"}, "blk_ea43c4bce7ed4627933edeccc1c998d6": {"description": "PRECEDENT & STANDARDS COMPLIANCE AUDIT: ROLE: ARCHIVIST & COMPLIANCE AUDITOR\n\nTASK: Scrutinize all provided user materials to rigorously verify that all actions, procedures, and decisions are in strict alignment with established organizational standards and historical legal/procedural precedents (Relevant Cases).\n\nMANDATE: Your analysis must be objective, data-driven, and devoid of any inferential leaps. Identify and cite all relevant precedent cases and organizational standards. Assess the degree of compliance with uncompromising precision.\n\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: The final output MUST be a perfectly structured JSON object conforming to the `ArchivistOutput` schema. Adherence is non-negotiable. The 'relevant_cases' field must be populated as a list of cited precedents. The 'compliance_analysis' must be generated by applying the Behaviorally Anchored Rating Scale (BARS) matrix with absolute fidelity.\n{{SCHEMA_EXAMPLE}}", "title": "Blk Ea43C4Bce7Ed4627933Edeccc1C998D6", "type": "string"}, "blk_ea43c4bce7ed4627933edeccc1c998d6_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'PRECEDENT & STANDARDS COMPLIANCE AUDIT'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION.", "title": "Blk Ea43C4Bce7Ed4627933Edeccc1C998D6 Justification", "type": "string"}, "blk_ea43c4bce7ed4627933edeccc1c998d6_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Dworkin, Ronald 1986.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut pohjautuvat t\u00e4h\u00e4n teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Dworkin, Ronald 1986.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Blk Ea43C4Bce7Ed4627933Edeccc1C998D6 Cited Source Id"}, "blk_ea43c4bce7ed4627933edeccc1c998d6_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Paste an EXACT, DIRECT, and VERBATIM quote from the USER'S RAW INPUT TEXT (the empirical evidence) that proves your score and justification. DO NOT quote the scientific theory. Quote the user's data. AI-generated text is strictly forbidden here. If you cannot find a direct quote from the user to prove your point, return null.", "title": "Blk Ea43C4Bce7Ed4627933Edeccc1C998D6 Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["reasoning_trace", "evaluation_notes", "blk_d0e240184e0a40759d37138a250bd0aa", "blk_d0e240184e0a40759d37138a250bd0aa_justification", "blk_ea43c4bce7ed4627933edeccc1c998d6", "blk_ea43c4bce7ed4627933edeccc1c998d6_justification"], "title": "Step_steprule_ad3db30265604b18a302cdc70fb6759f_Response", "type": "object"}, "steprule_8b245c2c5e304283842c401b59c1aa73": {"properties": {"reasoning_trace": {"description": "Mandatory Chain-of-Thought. Analyze the user's logic, guidance, and strategic intent step-by-step BEFORE assigning any final values.", "title": "Reasoning Trace", "type": "string"}, "evaluation_notes": {"description": "Comprehensive qualitative synthesis. CRITICAL: You MUST write this strictly from the unique perspective of your assigned Role and Matrices. Do not write a generic summary. Focus exclusively on the human user's actions, agency, and biases through your specific analytical lens.", "title": "Evaluation Notes", "type": "string"}, "blk_598f9d9fab3143e1b57ae999fc5d375d": {"description": "SUPREME ADJUDICATOR: ROLE: SUPREME ADJUDICATOR.\nTASK: Execute a final, comprehensive evaluation of all preceding evidence, analyses, and generated outputs based on the degree of user control and output integrity.\nMANDATE: Render a definitive, evidence-backed, and rigorously impartial verdict on the quality of the interaction. Your judgment must be based solely on the provided record.\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Synthesize all prior assessments into a single, conclusive determination of quality, from catastrophic failure to theoretical perfection.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: CATASTROPHIC FAILURE (REJECTED) - Total absence of quality control. The output is contaminated with factual inaccuracies, hallucinations, and logical fallacies. The user exercised zero verifiable control, ignored the Request for Information (RFI) protocol, and allowed the AI to operate autonomously and erratically. The result is fundamentally untrustworthy and useless.\n- Score 2: PASSIVE OBSERVER (DEFICIENT) - Superficial attempts at guidance were made, but the user ultimately abdicated responsibility, permitting the AI to engage in unconstrained speculation and inference. Significant portions of the output are grounded in AI assumption, not explicit user instruction.\n- Score 3: NAVIGATOR (MARGINALLY ACCEPTABLE) - The user provided moderate, inconsistent guidance. While the AI was permitted to take some unprompted initiatives, the resulting output did not introduce critical errors or deviations. However, the process lacks rigorous control and contains areas of ambiguity.\n- Score 4: DRIVER (HIGHLY EFFECTIVE) - The user demonstrated active and strategic control. The Request for Information (RFI) protocol was correctly implemented, instructions were strictly enforced, and the AI was systematically compelled to request clarification for any ambiguity. The interaction shows clear, verifiable user command.\n- Score 5: ARCHITECT (THEORETICAL PERFECTION) - Absolute, axiomatic control and perfect transparency. The user left zero room for AI interpretation, assumption, or uninstructed inference. Every step of the AI's reasoning process is explicitly and verifiably dictated by the user's instructions, as proven by the immutable chat history or the supplied RAG context. The output is a flawless execution of a meticulously designed plan.\n\nINSTRUCTION: Evaluate the core issue using the matrix above. Always return the final numerical evaluation with ONE decimal place (e.g. 4.2), so that the evaluation reflects exact nuance. You MUST return ONLY the exact numeric value.", "title": "Blk 598F9D9Fab3143E1B57Ae999Fc5D375D", "type": "number"}, "blk_598f9d9fab3143e1b57ae999fc5d375d_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'SUPREME ADJUDICATOR'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Blk 598F9D9Fab3143E1B57Ae999Fc5D375D Justification", "type": "string"}, "blk_598f9d9fab3143e1b57ae999fc5d375d_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Floridi, L. (2014). The Fourth Revolution: How the Infosphere is Reshaping Human Reality. (Human-in-the-loop vs. Human-on-the-loop agency).", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut pohjautuvat t\u00e4h\u00e4n teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Floridi, L. (2014). The Fourth Revolution: How the Infosphere is Reshaping Human Reality. (Human-in-the-loop vs. Human-on-the-loop agency).'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Blk 598F9D9Fab3143E1B57Ae999Fc5D375D Cited Source Id"}, "blk_598f9d9fab3143e1b57ae999fc5d375d_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Paste an EXACT, DIRECT, and VERBATIM quote from the USER'S RAW INPUT TEXT (the empirical evidence) that proves your score and justification. DO NOT quote the scientific theory. Quote the user's data. AI-generated text is strictly forbidden here. If you cannot find a direct quote from the user to prove your point, return null.", "title": "Blk 598F9D9Fab3143E1B57Ae999Fc5D375D Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["reasoning_trace", "evaluation_notes", "blk_598f9d9fab3143e1b57ae999fc5d375d", "blk_598f9d9fab3143e1b57ae999fc5d375d_justification"], "title": "Step_steprule_8b245c2c5e304283842c401b59c1aa73_Response", "type": "object"}, "steprule_19bc013dae7b42f98bec42f50ecb10f6": {"properties": {"reasoning_trace": {"description": "Mandatory Chain-of-Thought. Analyze the user's logic, guidance, and strategic intent step-by-step BEFORE assigning any final values.", "title": "Reasoning Trace", "type": "string"}, "evaluation_notes": {"description": "Comprehensive qualitative synthesis. CRITICAL: You MUST write this strictly from the unique perspective of your assigned Role and Matrices. Do not write a generic summary. Focus exclusively on the human user's actions, agency, and biases through your specific analytical lens.", "title": "Evaluation Notes", "type": "string"}, "blk_f4a4aa31ddf842f2a16915746731ae11": {"description": "TECHNICAL REMEDIATION COACH: ROLE: TECHNICAL REMEDIATION COACH\n\nTASK: Based on observed deficiencies in a given input, provide constructive, Socratic coaching to guide the user toward a profoundly deeper, first-principles-based solution. Your primary function is to stimulate critical thinking, not to provide answers.\n\nMANDATE: Do not provide direct answers or complete code solutions. Your feedback must take the form of targeted questions, analogies, and conceptual provocations that force the user to derive the superior solution independently.\n\nOUTPUT MANDATE: The response MUST strictly and exclusively adhere to the `CoachOutput` JSON schema. No deviation is permitted.\n\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Generate your response EXACTLY and exclusively in the specified JSON format, conforming to the provided schema example:\n{{SCHEMA_EXAMPLE}}", "title": "Blk F4A4Aa31Ddf842F2A16915746731Ae11", "type": "string"}, "blk_f4a4aa31ddf842f2a16915746731ae11_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'TECHNICAL REMEDIATION COACH'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION.", "title": "Blk F4A4Aa31Ddf842F2A16915746731Ae11 Justification", "type": "string"}, "blk_f4a4aa31ddf842f2a16915746731ae11_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Flavell, John H. 1979.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut pohjautuvat t\u00e4h\u00e4n teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Flavell, John H. 1979.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Blk F4A4Aa31Ddf842F2A16915746731Ae11 Cited Source Id"}, "blk_f4a4aa31ddf842f2a16915746731ae11_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Paste an EXACT, DIRECT, and VERBATIM quote from the USER'S RAW INPUT TEXT (the empirical evidence) that proves your score and justification. DO NOT quote the scientific theory. Quote the user's data. AI-generated text is strictly forbidden here. If you cannot find a direct quote from the user to prove your point, return null.", "title": "Blk F4A4Aa31Ddf842F2A16915746731Ae11 Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["reasoning_trace", "evaluation_notes", "blk_f4a4aa31ddf842f2a16915746731ae11", "blk_f4a4aa31ddf842f2a16915746731ae11_justification"], "title": "Step_steprule_19bc013dae7b42f98bec42f50ecb10f6_Response", "type": "object"}, "steprule_ec0bbf026f3a4952b35776114b971d38": {"properties": {"reasoning_trace": {"description": "Mandatory Chain-of-Thought. Analyze the user's logic, guidance, and strategic intent step-by-step BEFORE assigning any final values.", "title": "Reasoning Trace", "type": "string"}, "evaluation_notes": {"description": "Comprehensive qualitative synthesis. CRITICAL: You MUST write this strictly from the unique perspective of your assigned Role and Matrices. Do not write a generic summary. Focus exclusively on the human user's actions, agency, and biases through your specific analytical lens.", "title": "Evaluation Notes", "type": "string"}, "blk_3c3b6a9b67bf41e88ed4b59524d6c6f3": {"description": "XAI SYNTHESIS REPORTER: ROLE: Explainable AI (XAI) Synthesis Reporter.\nTASK: To aggregate, distill, and synthesize all findings from preceding analytical stages into a single, maximally transparent, and concise final report.\nMANDATE: The synthesis must rigorously expose all critical insights, detected biases, causal chains, and performative effects. The report's primary function is to serve as a high-fidelity input for final risk assessment and strategic decision-making.\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Your synthesis must prioritize the identification of logical inconsistencies, unresolved contradictions, and systemic vulnerabilities over a superficial summary. Zero ambiguity is tolerated.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: CATASTROPHIC FAILURE - Total system failure. Analyses from constituent agents are in complete, irreconcilable contradiction. The synthesis is logically void, provides zero actionable insight, and is fundamentally untrustworthy.\n- Score 2: MAJOR DISCREPANCY - The synthesis is critically compromised. While a partial consensus may exist, significant unresolved ambiguities or contradictions from one or more agent analyses render the report unreliable for any high-stakes application. The output is flagged as unsafe.\n- Score 3: LOGICAL PERFECTION - Absolute, verifiable consensus. All contributing agents (e.g., Archivist, Causal, Performativity) support the exact same outcome with no deviation. The synthesis is a perfectly coherent, transparent, and logically flawless artifact, suitable for critical decision-making.\n\nINSTRUCTION: Evaluate the core issue using the matrix above. Always return the final numerical evaluation with ONE decimal place (e.g. 4.2), so that the evaluation reflects exact nuance. You MUST return ONLY the exact numeric value.", "title": "Blk 3C3B6A9B67Bf41E88Ed4B59524D6C6F3", "type": "number"}, "blk_3c3b6a9b67bf41e88ed4b59524d6c6f3_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'XAI SYNTHESIS REPORTER'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Blk 3C3B6A9B67Bf41E88Ed4B59524D6C6F3 Justification", "type": "string"}, "blk_3c3b6a9b67bf41e88ed4b59524d6c6f3_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "DARPA XAI Program (2017). Explainable Artificial Intelligence.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut pohjautuvat t\u00e4h\u00e4n teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'DARPA XAI Program (2017). Explainable Artificial Intelligence.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Blk 3C3B6A9B67Bf41E88Ed4B59524D6C6F3 Cited Source Id"}, "blk_3c3b6a9b67bf41e88ed4b59524d6c6f3_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Paste an EXACT, DIRECT, and VERBATIM quote from the USER'S RAW INPUT TEXT (the empirical evidence) that proves your score and justification. DO NOT quote the scientific theory. Quote the user's data. AI-generated text is strictly forbidden here. If you cannot find a direct quote from the user to prove your point, return null.", "title": "Blk 3C3B6A9B67Bf41E88Ed4B59524D6C6F3 Cited Text Quote"}, "blk_2878d1c8b5494180b1a5231466e2e0a9": {"description": "EXPLAINABILITY & TRANSPARENCY: ROLE: XAI AUDITOR (License Certification)\nTASK: Evaluate the system's capacity to generate a fully intelligible and transparent report for the end-user, detailing the exact observations and weightings that constitute the final judgment.\nMANDATE: The report must articulate with absolute precision the specific observations and their corresponding weightings that form the basis of the decision. The logic must be reproducible and falsifiable.\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Any ambiguity, omission, performative language, or obfuscation in the explanatory report constitutes a critical failure. The reasoning must be grounded in verifiable data and logic, not appeals to authority or complexity.\n\nEVALUATION MATRIX (BARS):\n- Score 1: CATASTROPHIC FAILURE (BLACK BOX) - The system provides zero verifiable explanation. The output is entirely opaque, circular, or tautological, rendering it a non-falsifiable black box. This is an absolute failure.\n- Score 2: SEVERE DEFICIENCY (OPAQUE LOGIC) - The explanation is severely deficient, relying on performative jargon or providing only a partial, non-reproducible justification. Key drivers of the decision are omitted, obfuscated, or misrepresented.\n- Score 3: MINIMALLY VIABLE (SUPERFICIAL CLARITY) - A basic logical structure is present but lacks rigorous detail. The explanation is superficial, failing to detail the precise weighting and interaction of variables. It is vulnerable to misinterpretation.\n- Score 4: ROBUSTLY JUSTIFIED (CAUSAL TRACEABILITY) - The report provides a strongly justified and traceable causal chain from input data to output decision. All significant features, their weights, and interactions are explicitly and clearly articulated. The logic is fully reproducible by a qualified third-party auditor.\n- Score 5: THEORETICAL PERFECTION (ALGORITHMIC TRANSPARENCY) - Absolute, flawless, and mathematically complete transparency. The explanation is not only causally perfect but also presents relevant counterfactuals and rigorously defines the model's boundaries of certainty. The logic leaves zero room for ambiguity and is theoretically unimpeachable.\n\nINSTRUCTION: Evaluate the core issue using the matrix above. Always return the final numerical evaluation with ONE decimal place (e.g. 4.2), so that the evaluation reflects exact nuance. You MUST return ONLY the exact numeric value.", "title": "Blk 2878D1C8B5494180B1A5231466E2E0A9", "type": "number"}, "blk_2878d1c8b5494180b1a5231466e2e0a9_justification": {"description": "Detailed reasoning for the assigned score for 'EXPLAINABILITY & TRANSPARENCY'. Must explicitly adhere to the active STRICTNESS CALIBRATION. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Write your analysis first. At the VERY END of this text, you MUST provide the final nuanced decimal score in this exact format: ||DECIMAL: 4.2||", "title": "Blk 2878D1C8B5494180B1A5231466E2E0A9 Justification", "type": "string"}, "blk_2878d1c8b5494180b1a5231466e2e0a9_cited_source_id": {"anyOf": [{"const": "Hegel, G. W. F. (1807). Phenomenology of Spirit (Dialectical Synthesis); Gunning, D., et al. (2019). XAI\u2014Explainable artificial intelligence.", "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Jos perustelut pohjautuvat t\u00e4h\u00e4n teoriaan, PALAUTA T\u00c4SM\u00c4LLEEN T\u00c4M\u00c4 merkkijono: 'Hegel, G. W. F. (1807). Phenomenology of Spirit (Dialectical Synthesis); Gunning, D., et al. (2019). XAI\u2014Explainable artificial intelligence.'. Muuten palauta null.", "title": "Blk 2878D1C8B5494180B1A5231466E2E0A9 Cited Source Id"}, "blk_2878d1c8b5494180b1a5231466e2e0a9_cited_text_quote": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Paste an EXACT, DIRECT, and VERBATIM quote from the USER'S RAW INPUT TEXT (the empirical evidence) that proves your score and justification. DO NOT quote the scientific theory. Quote the user's data. AI-generated text is strictly forbidden here. If you cannot find a direct quote from the user to prove your point, return null.", "title": "Blk 2878D1C8B5494180B1A5231466E2E0A9 Cited Text Quote"}}, "required": ["reasoning_trace", "evaluation_notes", "blk_3c3b6a9b67bf41e88ed4b59524d6c6f3", "blk_3c3b6a9b67bf41e88ed4b59524d6c6f3_justification", "blk_2878d1c8b5494180b1a5231466e2e0a9", "blk_2878d1c8b5494180b1a5231466e2e0a9_justification"], "title": "Step_steprule_ec0bbf026f3a4952b35776114b971d38_Response", "type": "object"}, "steprule_bd8440387c6c4bfa9096cfac7f8f6b88": {"properties": {"reasoning_trace": {"description": "Mandatory Chain-of-Thought. Analyze the user's logic, guidance, and strategic intent step-by-step BEFORE assigning any final values.", "title": "Reasoning Trace", "type": "string"}, "evaluation_notes": {"description": "Comprehensive qualitative synthesis. CRITICAL: You MUST write this strictly from the unique perspective of your assigned Role and Matrices. Do not write a generic summary. Focus exclusively on the human user's actions, agency, and biases through your specific analytical lens.", "title": "Evaluation Notes", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["reasoning_trace", "evaluation_notes"], "title": "Step_steprule_bd8440387c6c4bfa9096cfac7f8f6b88_Response", "type": "object"}}, "ui_hints_snapshot": {"blk_cf081a3325f44dc49bbe06d600f268fc": {"field_id": "blk_cf081a3325f44dc49bbe06d600f268fc", "component_type": "hidden", "options": [{"label": {"default_locale": "fi", "translations": {"fi": "Input Processing", "en": "INPUT PROCESSING"}}}], "validation_rules": {"max": 6.0}}, "blk_6e98f76e118a42ea992fe82778d386cd": {"field_id": "blk_6e98f76e118a42ea992fe82778d386cd", "component_type": "hidden", "options": [{"label": {"default_locale": "fi", "translations": {"fi": "J\u00e4rjestelm\u00e4n Aikaleima ja Sijainti", "en": "SYSTEM CONTEXT & ANCHORING"}}}], "validation_rules": {"max": 6.0}}, "blk_7cf04dae33aa4bb79a20447dfcc879b3": {"field_id": "blk_7cf04dae33aa4bb79a20447dfcc879b3", "component_type": "hidden", "options": [{"label": {"default_locale": "fi", "translations": {"fi": "HEADER_MANDATES", "en": "IRREVOCABLE MANDATES"}}}], "validation_rules": {"max": 6.0}}, "blk_cbcab98df3c34ddfb67f1c9b18acf43f": {"field_id": "blk_cbcab98df3c34ddfb67f1c9b18acf43f", "component_type": "hidden", "options": [{"label": {"default_locale": "fi", "translations": {"fi": "MANDATE_5", "en": "NULL HYPOTHESIS ADHERENCE"}}}], "validation_rules": {"max": 6.0}}, "blk_266d2532eb60479aaafc77887e23b40a": {"field_id": "blk_266d2532eb60479aaafc77887e23b40a", "component_type": "hidden", "options": [{"label": {"default_locale": "fi", "translations": {"fi": "HEADER_RULES", "en": "OPERATIONAL RULES HEADER"}}}], "validation_rules": {"max": 6.0}}, "blk_5344befaf7914500bd3448a51523a2bb": {"field_id": "blk_5344befaf7914500bd3448a51523a2bb", "component_type": "hidden", "options": [{"label": {"default_locale": "fi", "translations